# ── PRODUCTION environment ────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this to .env for production deployments.
# Never commit .env to source control.

NODE_ENV=production

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8080
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Your production domain — used for CORS and sitemap
APP_URL=https://www.greenstreet.finance
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://www.greenstreet.finance,https://greenstreet.finance

# ── API authentication ────────────────────────────────────────
# verifyFirebaseToken (src/middleware/auth.ts) runs GLOBALLY on every /api/*
# route, but it only REJECTS unauthenticated requests when REQUIRE_AUTH=true.
# Left unset → most routes stay reachable anonymously. That is currently
# REQUIRED for part of the app to work:
#   - The SPA never attaches a Firebase ID token to its fetch() calls (there is
#     no getIdToken() anywhere in src/), so even signed-in users send no
#     Authorization header. Firebase login is a client-side gate only.
#   - The DSCR Analyzer is reachable before login via "Try demo" (demoMode),
#     and /api/dscr/* is pure local compute with no external cost.
#
# DO NOT simply set REQUIRE_AUTH=true here. It is global, so it would 401 EVERY
# unauthenticated request — breaking the analyzer for demo AND signed-in users —
# until the frontend is changed to send `Authorization: Bearer <idToken>`.
#
# /api/narrate is the ONE exception and is NOT open. It calls a paid LLM
# (ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN), so it is gated by its own separate, UNCONDITIONAL
# `requireAuth` guard (src/middleware/auth.ts, mounted only on this route in
# serverApp.ts) — it 401s any request with no verified req.user regardless of
# the REQUIRE_AUTH flag above, in every environment. No frontend code
# currently calls /api/narrate or attaches an ID token to reach it, so in
# practice it is only reachable today by a caller that explicitly sends
# `Authorization: Bearer <idToken>`. See src/routes/narrate.ts.
# REQUIRE_AUTH=true   # enable ONLY after the SPA attaches Firebase ID tokens

# ── Anthropic ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL must be set here in production, or /api/narrate 503s.
# This is deliberate, not a bug: there is no hardcoded third-party fallback,
# because narrate sends real borrower financial data to whatever host this
# resolves to, and picking a destination for that silently is not acceptable
# (see the API authentication note above and src/routes/narrate.ts). Narrate
# also 503s in any environment if ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is missing/placeholder.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Number of DSCR worker threads. Set to 0 for synchronous execution on
# memory-constrained serverless instances; defaults to 4 when unset.
# WORKER_POOL_SIZE=4

# ── Firebase (VITE_ prefix → exposed to browser bundle) ───────
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Server-only Firebase Admin credentials. Firebase Cloud Functions obtains
# Application Default Credentials automatically. For Vercel or another
# non-Google host, set this as an encrypted deployment secret so server-side
# lead intake and optional Firestore-backed rate limits can authenticate.
# Never prefix it with VITE_ and never commit its value.
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# ── Supabase (VITE_ prefix → exposed to browser bundle) ───────
# Use only the publishable/anon key. Never place a service-role key in VITE_*.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
